Treat /home/<user>/BBB_rootfs as root
	+ Install 'apt' and 'dpkg' libraries (*.so) for install new packages
	+ Install basic Debian packages for ARM by adding ../etc/apt/source.list
	+ Use installed initramfs-tools to build initramfs.img for custom BBB
	+ Include some basic seperate drivers (gpio-omap.ko) into initramfs.img to mount /dev/mmcblk0p1 to read and mount rootfilesystem
	
==============
If not including gpio-omap.ko => the boot process stucks at 'waiting for mounting root /dev/mmcblk0p1'
